  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Three teams – win the puck back at once",
  "description": "Split the group into three equal teams, for example three teams of three. Two teams play together (blue) and keep the puck against the third (red) inside an area marked with cones, roughly the neutral zone.\n\nWhen red win the puck the teams swap roles at once: red try to keep it as long as they can and blue must win it back within a few seconds. Count how many passes red manage. Change which team is on its own after a minute, and keep the shifts short.\n\nVariation: set up two cone goals at the ends of the area. If red win the puck they score by skating it through one of the cone goals. Blue may then leave the area to skate back and protect the cone goals.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest player goes straight at the puck carrier when the puck is lost – think three seconds."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The others close the nearest passing lanes so the pressured player cannot pass out of trouble."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you are beaten: skate back on the right side of the puck, between the puck and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "With the puck: make the area big and show for a pass with your stick on the ice."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
